---
description: Use the connected Mnemoverse memory before acting on project-specific work and save durable decisions afterwards
alwaysApply: false
---

A memory server is connected. Connecting it does not make it useful by itself; these standing rules do.

Recall before: starting work on a project you have touched before, choosing a library or pattern, writing tests or commits where conventions apply, answering "how do we usually do X here", anything phrased as "again" or "like last time". Search with the user's actual words plus the project name; if the first search returns nothing useful, try one broader query, then proceed without memory rather than looping.

Save when: a decision was made that will still matter next week, the user corrected you (the strongest signal there is), an approach failed and you know why, a preference outlives this task, or an environment fact was discovered the hard way. One memory, one fact. Never store secrets, tokens, payment data, or personal identifiers.

When something changes, the old fact is closed, not wrong: mark it superseded and write the new one alongside. If recall returns two entries that disagree, surface both with their dates instead of silently picking the closer match.
